<h1>darctan2</h1>
<p>This function returns the inverse tangent of an angle y/x, where <span class="inline">y = Opposite side of triangle</span> and <span class="inline">x = Adjacent side of triangle</span>. Unlike <a href="darctan.htm"><span class="inline">darctan()</span></a> the function <span class="inline">darctan2()</span> is valid for all angles and so may be used to convert a vector to an angle without risking division by zero, and it also returns a result in the correct quadrant.</p>
<p class="note"><b>NOTE</b>: The value returned is in degrees, not radians.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">darctan2(y, x);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>y</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The y coordinate to calculate.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>x</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The x coordinate to calculate.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">val = darctan2(1, 1);</p>
<p>This will set &quot;val&quot; to the correct angle.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
